; expect 32
; The expansion walk honors the definition-site stamp.
;
; A template-owned reference - a helper call, or a recursive self-call
; - is resolved where the macro was written, not where it is invoked:
; `substTpl` stamps every template free identifier (word 10), and the
; walk (`expandApp`, `expandVarRef`) looks the macro up even when the
; caller binds the same spelling. Letting the caller's `let` win made
; the invocation stop expanding: the unexpanded call survived a check
; that said OK, and `opt` died on a symbol nothing defined.
;
;   entry  this file's own helper pair, invoked under a shadowing
;          local: 5 + 1.
;   module `DefScopeWalk.pick3`, a recursive self-call, invoked
;          qualified under a shadowing local: the else branch.
;   helper `DefScopeWalk.viaHelper`, whose template calls the
;          module's own `addOne`, invoked under a shadowing local.
(import DefScopeWalk)

(emacro inner ((inner x) (+ x 1)))

(emacro outer ((outer x) (inner x)))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (+
    (+
      (let ((inner 100))
        (outer 5))
      (let ((pick3 99))
        (DefScopeWalk::pick3
          (== 1 2)
          10
          (== 1 1)
          20
          30)))
    (let ((addOne 1000))
      (DefScopeWalk::viaHelper 5))))
